statement:
Let $I$ be a directed set and $(X_i,f_{i'i})$ an inverse system of schemes [def-pc-scheme] over $I$ whose transition morphisms $f_{i'i}:X_{i'}\to X_i$ ($i'\ge i$) are affine [pqf-def-affine-morphism], every $X_i$ being quasi-compact and quasi-separated [def-weil-pbc-scheme-conventions]; let $X=\varprojlim_iX_i$ with projections $f_i:X\to X_i$ [lem-weil-pbc-limit-affine-transition]. For $i\in I$, an $X_i$-scheme $V$ and $i'\ge i$ write $V_{i'}=V\times_{X_i}X_{i'}$ and $V_X=V\times_{X_i}X$ (fibre products [def-pc-fibre-product] along $f_{i'i}$ and $f_i$), and $\psi_{i'}$, $\psi_X$ for the base changes of an $X_i$-morphism $\psi$. An $X$-scheme (or $X_i$-scheme) is *etale of finite presentation* if its structure morphism is etale [def-weil-etale-morphism] and of finite presentation, i.e. locally of finite presentation, quasi-compact and quasi-separated [def-weil-pbc-scheme-conventions]. A *finite diagram* of such $X$-schemes consists of a finite set $A$ of $X$-schemes $U^a$ ($a\in A$) etale of finite presentation, a finite set $E$ of $X$-morphisms $\psi_e:U^{s(e)}\to U^{t(e)}$ ($s,t:E\to A$), and a finite set $R$ of relations, each an equality between the composites of two chains of the $\psi_e$ with the same source and target (an empty chain at $a$ standing for $\mathrm{id}_{U^a}$). Then:

1. *(objects)* for every $X$-scheme $U$ etale of finite presentation there are $i\in I$, an $X_i$-scheme $U_i$ etale of finite presentation and an isomorphism of $X$-schemes $U\cong(U_i)_X$;
2. *(morphisms)* given $i\in I$, $X_i$-schemes $U_i,V_i$ etale of finite presentation and an $X$-morphism $\psi:(U_i)_X\to(V_i)_X$, there are $i'\ge i$ and an $X_{i'}$-morphism $\psi_{i'}:(U_i)_{i'}\to(V_i)_{i'}$ whose base change to $X$ is $\psi$ (through the canonical isomorphisms $((U_i)_{i'})_X\cong(U_i)_X$, $((V_i)_{i'})_X\cong(V_i)_X$);
3. *(equalities)* given $i$, such $U_i,V_i$ and two $X_i$-morphisms $\psi,\chi:U_i\to V_i$ with $\psi_X=\chi_X$, there is $i'\ge i$ with $\psi_{i'}=\chi_{i'}$;
4. *(finite diagrams)* for every finite diagram $(A,E,R)$ as above there are $i\in I$, $X_i$-schemes $U^a_i$ etale of finite presentation ($a\in A$), $X_i$-morphisms $\psi_{e,i}:U^{s(e)}_i\to U^{t(e)}_i$ ($e\in E$) satisfying every relation of $R$, and isomorphisms of $X$-schemes $\alpha_a:(U^a_i)_X\to U^a$ with $\alpha_{t(e)}\circ(\psi_{e,i})_X=\psi_e\circ\alpha_{s(e)}$ for all $e\in E$ (a *descended diagram at stage $i$*); its base change to any $i'\ge i$ (the $(U^a_i)_{i'}$, the $(\psi_{e,i})_{i'}$ and the $\alpha_a$ composed with $((U^a_i)_{i'})_X\cong(U^a_i)_X$) is a descended diagram at stage $i'$;
5. *(coverings)* in a descended diagram at stage $i$ as in 4, let $b\in A$ and $B\subseteq E$ with $t(e)=b$ for all $e\in B$ be such that $\{\psi_e:U^{s(e)}\to U^b\}_{e\in B}$ is a covering in $X_{\Et}$ [def-weil-pbc-etale-site]. Then there is $i_1\ge i$ such that for every $i'\ge i_1$ the family $\{(\psi_{e,i})_{i'}:(U^{s(e)}_i)_{i'}\to(U^b_i)_{i'}\}_{e\in B}$ is a covering in $(X_{i'})_{\Et}$.
